      "id": "sol.amc-8-1991-p12.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "The left side is \\(\\dfrac{9}{3} = 3.\\) The right side is \\(\\dfrac{5973}{N},\\) and setting it equal to \\(3\\) gives \\(N = 1991.\\)\n\nEquivalently, \\((k-1) + k + (k+1) = 3k,\\) so dividing by \\(3\\) leaves the middle term. Here the middle term is \\(1991.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is D .",
      "hints": [
        "Simplify the left side first",
        "The sum of three consecutive integers divided by the middle one equals \\(3\\)"
      ],
